Your travel & hotel details

Hi Dartmouth team,

We=E2=80=99re looking forward to welcoming you to Brown for IIC on November 5=
=E2=80=936. Your outbound journey, hotel details, and return journey are belo=
w. All times are Eastern Time.

Your Dartmouth Coach tickets have been purchased. Purchase the MBTA portion s=
eparately; it does not require an advance reservation. Have your carrier tick=
ets available when boarding. These cards are itinerary summaries, not boardin=
g tickets.

To Providence =E2=80=94 Thursday, November 5



Dartmouth Coach =E2=80=94 ticket purchased



DEPARTURE

7:40 AM

Hanover
Dartmouth College, in front of Hopkins Center for the Arts


ARRIVAL

10:25 AM

South Station Bus Terminal
700 Atlantic Avenue, Boston



Arrive by 7:10 AM. Dartmouth Coach operates first come, first board; the purc=
hased ticket does not reserve a seat.

At South Station, walk from the bus terminal to the Commuter Rail concourse. =
The MBTA connection does not require an advance reservation; choose one of th=
e options below based on when the bus arrives.
MBTA Providence Line 6011 =E2=80=94 option 1



DEPARTURE

10:35 AM

Boston South Station


ARRIVAL

11:45 AM

Providence Station (PVD)



Only take this train if the bus arrives on time and you have enough time to r=
each the rail platform safely. The scheduled transfer is just 10 minutes.


MBTA Providence Line 6013 =E2=80=94 option 2



DEPARTURE

11:20 AM

Boston South Station


ARRIVAL

12:35 PM

Providence Station (PVD)



Use this option if the bus is delayed or the earlier connection would be rush=
ed.


View the November 5 MBTA timetable (https://www.mbta.com/schedules/CR-Provide=
nce/timetable?date=3D2026-11-05). Select a Providence-bound train, not a trai=
n terminating at Stoughton.




Your hotel



The Graduate

11 Dorrance Street
Providence, RI 02903

Check-in
Thursday, November 5
12:00 PM (noon) ET
Check-out
Friday, November 6
9:00 AM ET


Two rooms per team, with two participants per room.

If you take the 11:20 AM train, you will reach Providence at 12:35 PM. Please=
 head to the hotel after you arrive and let us know which connection you take.



Return =E2=80=94 Friday, November 6



MBTA Providence Line 6026 =E2=80=94 recommended



DEPARTURE

2:05 PM

Providence Station (PVD)


ARRIVAL

3:21 PM

Boston South Station



This uses the special November 6 construction timetable.


Plan to leave the closing lunch around 1:25 PM and be at Providence Station b=
y 1:45 PM.

Walk to the South Station bus terminal at 700 Atlantic Avenue. The scheduled =
connection gives you 69 minutes before the bus; join the Dartmouth Coach boar=
ding line by 4:00 PM.
Dartmouth Coach =E2=80=94 ticket purchased



DEPARTURE

4:30 PM

South Station Bus Terminal
700 Atlantic Avenue, Boston


ARRIVAL

7:30 PM

Hanover
Dartmouth College, in front of Hopkins Center for the Arts



Bus boarding is first come, first board. Keep your actual Dartmouth Coach tic=
ket available.




Every participant should bring a government-issued ID for travel and a studen=
t ID for check-in on arrival.

MBTA service is adjusted on November 6. The return times above follow the off=
icial construction timetable (https://cdn.mbta.com/sites/default/files/media/=
route_pdfs/2026-11-6-cr-providence-stoughton-line-construction-schedule.pdf).=
 Please check service alerts again before traveling.

Please reply if any of these details look incorrect, if your plans have chang=
ed, or if you run into a delay on the day.

Best,
The IIC Team





